+### Card audio: the script and the voice (owner decisions 2026-11-17; branch `feat/audio-build`)
+
+The Audio row's pill plays a spoken **add-on** to the card, not a read-aloud of it: it says what the card does not (the idea learners most often get wrong, one or two other examples, a misconception, what to try next). It is made in two paid steps, so the card is never delayed and nothing is spent on a card nobody plays.
+
+| Step | When | Route (control plane `explanation-audio.js`) | Provider | Result |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| Script | Right after a NEW written Explanation is on the canvas (`AdaptiveCanvas.jsx` `insertBlock`, never awaited; only in the owner's editable canvas, once per card id; a card loaded from a saved board is never asked) | `POST /api/learn/explanation-audio/script` `{ app, id, title, body, more?, depth, question? }` -> `{ script, transcript, seconds_estimate, scriptBy }` or `{ script: null, outcome, reason }` (still 200) | ONE call on the `google-low` chain profile: Gemini 3.5 Flash Lite, then Fireworks gpt-oss-120b (low) on an error | `block.narration = { status: 'script', script, transcript, seconds, scriptBy }`, or `{ status: 'error', failed: 'script', code, reason }` |
+| Voice | The owner's FIRST Play (`GeneratePill` in `ExplanationAudio.jsx` calls the host's `narrate`) | `POST /api/learn/explanation-audio/voice` `{ app, id, script, confirmed: true }` -> `{ narration }` | ElevenLabs `eleven_flash_v2_5`, voice Jessica (`cgSgspJ2msm6clMCkdW9`), `stability 0.4, similarity_boost 0.75, speed 1.1`, `mp3_44100_64` | `block.narration = { status: 'ready', fileRef, seconds, script, transcript, provider: 'elevenlabs', model: 'eleven_flash_v2_5', voiceId }`, or `{ status: 'error', failed: 'audio', code, reason }` with the script kept |
+
+- **Fields.** `script` is the only text the voice gets; `transcript` is the same sentences with every equation and number as LaTeX between dollars (what the transcript window shows). `seconds` is a words / 3 estimate until the voice exists, then the file's own length (bytes at 64 kbps). `scriptBy` is the script model; `provider`, `model` and `voiceId` are the voice. The server writes no board: the client lands each answer on the card (`explanation-audio.js` `landNarration`, a quiet update), and the board's normal save registers `narration.fileRef` (`file-refs.js`), so a share or publication link plays it.
+- **Length by Depth.** Brief about 60 to 80 s (180 to 240 words), Balanced about 90 s (240 to 300), Detailed up to about 2 minutes (300 to 360). Soft: the prompt says never pad. The script model is told the card's own Depth (`block.depth`); Gemini gets the higher word block that AUD-2 measured (it undershoots by about a quarter), Fireworks the plain one.
+- **Style.** The script mirrors the card's own register, vocabulary and rhythm (the prompt's STYLE section); no added enthusiasm.
+- **Prompt.** `explanation-audio-script.js` `scriptSystem` is AUD-2's v1.1 (`docs/features/explain/checks/aud-2/prompt-v1.1.txt`, root causes in `why.md`) with these changes: the numbers rule is the owner's (only numbers that appear in the card or its visuals, never compute; this ends v1.1's tension with its reuse rule); the answer is `{script, transcript}`; Detailed stops at about 2 minutes; the LaTeX delimiter is written by code so the source carries no money-looking text.
+- **Number safety (deterministic, no model).** After the script returns, every number it speaks (digits, and spelled-out words such as "zero point three six eight") must be a number of the card (its prose, the learner's question, every label and value inside its diagrams, in digits or words). A sentence that speaks any other number, or a script sentence that carries a symbol (`= + * / ^ < > [ ] %` and the like), is removed from the script and the transcript together (paired by position when they have the same sentence count; else each on its own). No regenerate, no retry. A lone "one" is not read as a number (it is also the pronoun). A script left under 40 words is an error (`too_short`): no audio worth voicing. Measured offline on AUD-2's real model outputs (the build README): Gemini V6 loses at least one sentence in 4 of 9 scripts (mean 1.2 of 12.4 sentences, 220 to 195 words), Fireworks V5 in 7 of 9 (2.4 of 14.2, 290 to 245 words).
+- **Money.** The script is platform-funded work the learner did not press for: usage feature `explanation_script` (in `FREE_FEATURES`: recorded, never charged), priced at the registry's Gemini or Fireworks rows by `spendTransport`. The voice is the learner's own Play: usage feature `explanation_audio` (charged, `would_charge`), admitted by `elevenSpendTransport` (`learn-paid-transport.js`) at the registry row `elevenlabs | eleven_flash_v2_5 | input_chars` (an estimate row: the list price is per 1,000 characters and the bill is plan credits), behind the paid confirmation (`paidRefusal`: the press sends `confirmed: true`). About 0.3 cent for a script and 1.7 to 7 cents for a voice of 430 to 1,800 characters.
+- **Guards.** Per-user hour and day caps (`admitUsage`, categories `explanation_script` 60 / 200 and `explanation_audio` 30 / 100; a worker var of the same name, for example `EXPLANATION_AUDIO_HOUR`, overrides one) counted only when a real call is about to be made; the platform spend guard and the learner's allowance (`admitSpend`); owner-only access (`authorizedBoardApp` then `subscriptionOwnerRefusal`), so a visitor of a shared or published canvas has no route to either call and the pill draws only for a ready narration (`ExplanationHost.narrate` exists only where the card can be edited).
+- **Idempotency.** One script per (org, canvas, card id) in the isolate, and two requests in flight share one call. The voice is kept as a file source of the board's owner under a deterministic id from (org, canvas, card id, script hash): a second Play, or a click while it is generating, finds the file or shares the in-flight call and is not billed twice. A retry runs only the step that failed (the pill's error state; a failed voice keeps its script).
+- **Failure never reaches the card.** A provider failure, a refused admission, a missing key (`not_configured`) or no storage is an answer with `status: 'error'` and a short `reason`; the pill shows its existing failed state and a notice says why (`toast`). Logs (`explanation_audio`) carry step, outcome, provider, word and character counts, never card text.
+- **Not built (v1, owner decisions):** an overlap check, a verifier or fact check, a model retry or regenerate, a script edit, other voices, regenerating a card's audio, audio for a card that already exists (only a new card asks for a script), and a cross-isolate lock for the voice call (two tabs pressing Play within the same seconds can bill twice; the file id keeps one file). An old narration with `status: 'failed'` still draws nothing.
+- **Checks:** `packages/control-plane/test/explanation-audio.test.js` (fake providers, in-memory D1 and R2), `packages/web/src/explanation-audio-client.test.mjs` and the new cases of `explanation-audio.test.mjs`.
